1. Have you used separate small partition for benchmarking? Disk =
performance varies about 2x times across the plate....

2. 596 and even 700MB/sec makes me think you measure not real disk I/O, =
but memory (cache).

3. iozone is not a trustable benchmark, it really sucks.

4. VMs may have wrong time flow inside the guest which may be slower =
then real wall clocks. So it takes sometimes "less" time for benchmark =
to complete and obviously performance results "faster".

5. VMs and containers are comparable on 1 rotational HDD. VM overhead =
becomes much more visible on fast SSD or SAN drives where performance =
can get as high as >1GB/sec.

Thanks,
Kirill


